nido.verifyBody:
Ask {{name}} to open “My code” in their NIDO and read their fingerprint aloud, in person or on a call where you recognize their voice.

It has to be exactly:
{{theirs}}

Your fingerprint, for {{name}} to check:
{{mine}}

Mark it only if they match. If they don’t, don’t trust this contact: someone could be in the middle.

agentConfirm.pairMessage:
Pair with “{{name}}”?
Fingerprint: {{fingerprint}}

Only confirm if you scanned this code in person.

agentConfirm.pairAmbiguousAsk:
This code is for “{{name}}” (fingerprint {{fingerprint}}), but you already have {{count}} live contact(s) with that name under a DIFFERENT identity: {{candidates}}. A name is not an identity — I cannot assume this is the same person.

Tell me explicitly (in chat):
• “replace” — the same person with a new device: removes the old identity from your contact list (destructive);
• “different person” — a different person: give me a unique name for the new contact;
• “cancel” — do nothing.

If you don't choose, I cancel. Nothing has been paired yet.

agentConfirm.pairReplaceConfirmMessage:
REPLACE the identity of “{{name}}”?
Fingerprint: {{fingerprint}}

This removes the old identity from this session's contact list. Any messages you had in the outbox for this name stay in the outbox under the same name. This cannot be undone. Confirm only if you verified this code in person.

agentConfirm.pairDifferentPersonConfirmMessage:
Pair “{{name}}” as a DIFFERENT PERSON named “{{newName}}”?
Fingerprint: {{fingerprint}}

Both identities stay live. Confirm only if you scanned this code in person.
